   - In WordPress, go to the "Settings" > "Reading" and ensure that "Allow traffic from..." is set to the appropriate origin(s).

   - Alternatively, you can add custom headers to the `functions.php` file of your WordPress theme or child theme:
     ```php
     function allow_cors() {
       header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *');
       header("Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE");
       header("Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization, X-Requested-With");
     }
     add_action( 'wp_headers', 'allow_cors' );
     ```

